index 2393dec..77041dc 100644
--- a/docs/examples.md
+++ b/docs/examples.md
@@ -497,6 +497,27 @@ This behavior can be changed using the *on_setattr* argument.
 
 Check out {ref}`converters` for more details.
 
+## Running Custom Code Before/After Setting Attributes
+
+An *on_setattr* hook can be a generator function that yields exactly once.
+The code before the `yield` runs before the attribute is set, the yielded value is used as the new value, and the code after the `yield` runs once the attribute has been set:
+
+```{doctest}
+>>> def gen_hook(instance, attribute, value):
+...     print(f"setting x to {value}")
+...     yield int(value) * 2 + 286
+...     print(f"set x to {instance.x}")
+>>> @define
+... class C:
+...     x: int = field(on_setattr=gen_hook)
+>>> c = C(42)
+>>> c.x = "67"
+setting x to 67
+set x to 420
+>>> c.x
+420
+```
+
